        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 1:17PM MDT by NWS Great Falls MT</headline>
        <description>Gusty to strong westerly winds will develop over much of central
and north-central Montana by this evening. The combination of the
frontal passage with isolated shower and thunderstorm activity
will result in brief instances of wind gusts exceeding 50 mph.

These winds may cause more damage to trees and power lines than
what is normally observed due to most trees being fully leafed out
and some trees being weakened by previous storms. Additionally,
any damaged tree branches may break loose and become projectiles.

Pedestrians and those outdoors should watch for flying debris and
avoid being near trees if possible during times of stronger
winds. Also, those traveling along north to south oriented
roadways should be prepared for strong cross winds.
</description>
